<title>USA: Mashpee, Mass., $30 mln repriced and restructured.</title>
<headline>Mashpee, Mass., $30 mln repriced and restructured.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>State Street Bank and Trust Co said Wednesday it repriced and restructured Mashpee, Mass.'s $30.3 million bond deal, raising the top yield in 2017 to 5.67 percent from 5.65 percent.</p>
<p>The repricing follows:  </p>
<p>TOWN OF MASHPEE, MASSACHUSETTS</p>
<p>RE: $30,360,000*</p>
<p>GENERAL OBLIGATION BONDS</p>
<p>VERBAL AWARD.</p>
<p>  MOODY'S: Aaa / A2	  S&amp;P: NR		    FITCH: AAA</p>
<p>MBIA INSURED</p>
<p>  DATED: 02/01/1997	  FIRST COUPON: 08/01/1997</p>
<p>DUE: 02/01</p>
<p> MATURITY		AMOUNT*    COUPON	   PRICE</p>
<p>02/01/1998		1,570M    4.50  %	  NRO</p>
<p>02/01/1999		1,570M    4.50  %	  NRO</p>
<p>02/01/2000		1,570M    4.30  %	  4.30</p>
<p>02/01/2001		1,570M    4.40  %	  4.40</p>
<p>02/01/2002		1,570M    4.50  %	  4.50</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>02/01/2003		1,565M    4.60  %	  4.60</p>
